# The Wi-Fi power-cycle test (RC_JOBS=rc.jobs.wifipower), on the jb system image so that Sileo
# can be opened first: an application in front that sets idleTimerDisabled is the one thing that
# reliably keeps SpringBoard from locking the display -- PM timers held and injected touches did
# not (logs/095245-run.log, logs/100719-run.log), and a locked display suspends the job with it.
# Then: join, the radio's power off and on, and an address and a name again with no joinfile
# between them -- the station layer's own re-join of the standing network.
/redwood/bin/sleep_hold 300 &
/var/jb/usr/bin/uiopen sileo://package/wget
/redwood/bin/rwtouch wait 25
/redwood/bin/net_test wait 30 joinfile /redwood/fw/network
/redwood/bin/net_test waitaddr en0 60 resolve apt.procurs.us
/redwood/bin/net_test power 0
/redwood/bin/net_test wait 5
/redwood/bin/net_test power 1
/redwood/bin/net_test wait 10
/redwood/bin/net_test waitaddr en0 60
/redwood/bin/net_test resolve apt.procurs.us
